Description: Fix CVE-2026-54514 SSRF via InetSocketAddress DNS resolution during deserialization
 jackson-databind's FromStringDeserializer constructed InetSocketAddress instances using
 the constructor that performs eager DNS resolution during deserialization. An application
 binding untrusted JSON into a type containing an InetSocketAddress field would issue an
 attacker-chosen DNS query during readValue, before any application-level validation.
 Switch to InetSocketAddress.createUnresolved(host, port), postponing DNS lookup until
 an explicit connect occurs.
 .
 Upstream fix 1f5a1037 modifies a single _inetSocketAddress(host, port) helper that was
 introduced after 2.13.3; in 2.13.3 the three call sites still inline the unsafe
 constructor, so each is rewritten directly. Test changes from the upstream commit are
 adapted to JUnit 3 / TestCase assertion style used in the 2.13.x test base.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/commit/1f5a1037b1e9e05920e755cb35f198bcd46667e4
Bug: https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-databind/security/advisories/GHSA-hgj6-7826-r7m5
Author: Tatu Saloranta <tatu.saloranta@iki.fi>
Last-Update: 2026-06-25

